From eeed324b36cfef9b3a56836c113af93fe9cdd29b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 16:19:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/29] droidian: build for aarch64-linux-gnu, not
 aarch64-linux-android

This 4.14 Makefile passes --target=$(notdir $(CROSS_COMPILE)) to clang, so
the packaging's aarch64-linux-android- triplet built the kernel for the
Android target.  With CC_STACKPROTECTOR_STRONG clang then reads the stack
canary from TPIDR_EL0 the way bionic lays it out; in the kernel that
register holds nothing yet, the first protected function takes the
__stack_chk_fail path before any console or restart handler exists, and
the phone sits on the boot logo.

Found by elimination on the phone with a reset probe: the same tree and
.config built with make and CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-gnu- gets past
setup_arch, the packaged build never does.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 debian/kernel-info.mk | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/debian/kernel-info.mk b/debian/kernel-info.mk
index ea18e534e..ae66e5093 100644
--- a/debian/kernel-info.mk
+++ b/debian/kernel-info.mk
@@ -206,7 +206,7 @@ BUILD_CROSS = 1
 # (Cross-build only) The build triplet to use. You'll probably want to
 # use aarch64-linux-android- if building Android kernels.
 # might need to use aarch64-linux-gnu- with newer kernels such as GKI
-BUILD_TRIPLET = aarch64-linux-android-
+BUILD_TRIPLET = aarch64-linux-gnu-
 
 # (Cross-build only) The build triplet to use with clang. You'll probably
 # want to use aarch64-linux-gnu- here.
-- 
